      Canonical schema identifier:
      https://lxndigital.com/id/schema/emissions/1.0.1

      Canonical schema location:
      https://lxndigital.com/schemas/emissions/1.0/Emissions-Schema-V1.0.1.xsd

      IANA Private Enterprise Number: 66369
      Enterprise OID: 1.3.6.1.4.1.66369
      Lifecycle Continuity OID: 1.3.6.1.4.1.66369.7
      Emissions Guidance Family OID: 1.3.6.1.4.1.66369.7.2
      Schema Family OID: 1.3.6.1.4.1.66369.7.2.2
      Schema Edition OID: 1.3.6.1.4.1.66369.7.2.2.1.1.0.1
      Schema Edition OID URN: urn:oid:1.3.6.1.4.1.66369.7.2.2.1.1.0.1

      EventEmissions is not a standalone business object. Its context is the
      enclosing EPCIS event. Event identity, products, quantities, input and
      output relationships, parties, locations, times, business steps,
      dispositions and transactions are inherited from that event and are not
      repeated here.

      The extension has four mutually exclusive record types.
      CradleToGateCheckpoint is a cumulative product carbon footprint result at
      a product-responsible organisation's outbound gate. It is normally placed
      on an EPCIS event whose business step is shipping or consigning, or on
      departing where the granular GS1 outbound pattern replaces shipping. It
      includes all upstream and organisation-attributable product emissions
      through that gate and replaces all earlier emissions inside its boundary.
      The checkpoint is the declared cumulative PCF only. Direct and purchased-
      energy activity occurring after it is recorded separately and is never
      inserted into or added twice within the checkpoint.

      DirectEmissionsContribution and PurchasedEnergyEmissionsContribution are
      incremental, product-attributable results for qualifying physical
      activities. For facility-based activities, the enclosing EPCIS event's
      bizLocation anchors the physical facility and SourceOfTruthRef identifies
      the Facility-activity operator and the applicable source-control or
      energy-purchase or procurement basis. For transporting activities,
      SourceOfTruthRef identifies the Transport-leg operator, the transport
      activity boundary and the applicable responsibility basis. No LCS
      authoring field is required.

      LogisticsFootprintContribution is an incremental, product-attributable
      life-cycle greenhouse-gas result for one physical logistics activity after
      an applicable outbound checkpoint and before the next product-responsible
      receiving boundary. Emissions Guidance V1.0.1 defines the permitted and
      prohibited business steps. The XSD cannot inspect the enclosing EPCIS
      business step, commercial segment or duplicate-event state; those are
      mandatory semantic conformance rules.

      Each record states a result in kgCO2e and a deterministic DeclaredUnit.
      DeclaredUnit is either Count, for a positive whole number of selected
      instances, or Measure plus Uom, where Uom is a two- or three-character
      UN/CEFACT Recommendation 20 Common Code for length, area, volume or mass.
      Implementations must validate the code against Recommendation 20 Annexes
      Revision 17 (2021), reject status X or D, and reject other quantity types.
      A later code-list revision may be used only where an exchange profile names
      it and all participants apply it consistently. Packaging levels such as
      pack, case and pallet are EPCIS
      identities, not free-text units: one selected pack, case or pallet is
      represented as Count 1. This quantity convention follows international
      trade and EPCIS quantity semantics; it is not derived from a PACT PCF data
      exchange unit enumeration.

      AppliesToIdentifier, when present, selects an EPC, EPC class, quantity
      class or parent identifier present in the enclosing event or
      deterministically resolved in its containment state. SourceOfTruthRef
      identifies the versioned calculation and evidence needed to test
      methodological compatibility before arithmetic addition.

      Corporate Scope 1, Scope 2 and Scope 3 classifications are reporter-
      relative and intentionally outside this schema. DirectEmissionsContribution
      and PurchasedEnergyEmissionsContribution are activity-source
      classifications, not universal corporate-inventory labels. Corporate
      Scope and Reporting-organisation-relative treatment are determined outside
      the schema using the explicit analytical context and responsibility
      evidence defined in Emissions Guidance V1.0.1. XML conformance requires
      the XSD plus the semantic rules in that guidance. JSON-LD is outside the
      normative conformance scope of this edition.
    </xs:documentation>
    <xs:appinfo source="https://lxndigital.com/id/schema/emissions/1.0.1">
      canonicalIdentifier=https://lxndigital.com/id/schema/emissions/1.0.1;
